course: dictionary
lesson: 558
title: Auction
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An auction is a public sale where things go to the person who offers the most money. People make bids, which are offers of money, and the bids rise higher and higher until nobody wants to go higher. Then the item is sold.
explain: Context helps you here. «Very high art prices come from fame, history, rarity and buyers competing at auctions» tells you that buyers compete with each other, so the price goes up. Auction is also a verb: to auction something means to sell it at an auction, and «auction off» means the same.
explain: In maths, auction problems ask you to compare bids: which bid is the highest, and how much more one bid is than another. Look for the word bid and the amounts of money, then compare them carefully.
fact: An auction is a public sale where things go to the person who offers the most money.
fact: To auction something, or auction it off, means to sell it at an auction.
fact: An online auction is held on a website, where people bid until a set time ends.
fact: The auctioneer is the person who runs an auction, and may call out «Going, going, gone!»
fact: Charity auctions raise money for good causes, and in 2018 one of Banksy's paintings partly shredded itself right after it sold at auction.
exercise: In «Rare Ming porcelain can sell for millions at auction», what does at auction mean? | *In a public sale, sold to the highest bidder | In a museum, where it is kept safe | Given away free to a friend
exercise: Ana bids 40 pounds and Ben bids 55 pounds at an auction. Who has the highest bid, and by how much? | Ana, by 15 pounds | Ben, by 95 pounds | *Ben, by 15 pounds | Ana, by 5 pounds
exercise: Ella hears the auctioneer say «Going, going, gone!» What has happened? | *The item has been sold | The bidding has stopped for lunch | The painting has gone to a museum | The auction has just started
test: Which is true about an online auction? | It is a sale in a shop where nobody makes bids | It is a race to see who runs fastest | *It is held on a website, where people bid until a set time ends | It is held only in schools and never online
test: What does «auction it off» mean? | To give it away to a friend | To keep it for ever in a museum | *To sell it at an auction | To paint a picture of it
exam: Which word names the person who runs an auction? | Bidder | Museum guard | Buyer | *Auctioneer
